ndencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nVersion: v4.5.1.stable.mono.official [f62fdbde1]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8129) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing `HeightMapShape3D` for collision causes rapid wobbling / bouncing look when the parent CollisionShape3D is scaled down (scaled down to 0.25 for my case). According to the [latest ](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_heightmapshape3d.html) docs, scaling the parent CollisionShape3D is the only way to adjust the scale of HeightMapShape3D.\n\nThis seems to make HeightMapShape3D completely unusable if you need any scale less than 1 as the \"resolution\" cannot be adjusted by any other means (that I can find, the docs are quite lacking for this object).\n\nThis happens with both Jolt physics and Godot physics, but it's worse with Godot as the object never seems to settle, whereas jolt just wobbles for a moment then stops, but both give a very undesirable look.\n\nEdit: Tested a little more. Scaling to 2 results in the cube settling unevenly, 1.25 does similar. So it seems even scaling up, and scaling by a factor of 1 also does not behave right.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a CollisionShape3D and use a HeightMapShape3D as the shape, any size seems to work, and the data can all be default (all 0 / completely flat).\n\nCreate a RigidBody3D with a cube shape and drop it so it collides at an angle with the HeightMapShape3D. If it falls perfectly flat it does not seem to happen so must tilt the cube a bit.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[height-map-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24655288/height-map-test.zip)\n\nSimply run it and you should see it wobble rapidly before it stops moving, change the scale of the CollisionShape3D back to 1 makes it work normally again.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115009/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115009/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}